From 92fae1541cc6f53d698925feefdd03096061f553 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 01:11:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Admin: User journey map
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A new admin module, Product → User journey (/admin/user-journey), ported
from the owner's journey blueprint page: four stages (Reflect, Create,
Experience, Share) with their guiding question, illustrated moments with
the feature each suggests, and product screens in phone frames. Filter by
layer and stage, zoom, edit a moment or screen (title, description,
feature, image upload resized in the browser), add and delete, rename
stages, export and import JSON (the original page's export too), restore
the original. Edits persist in this browser through lib/storage, like the
rest of the admin.

The data and its helpers live in admin/data/userJourney.ts with tests.
Illustrations are resized from about 2 MB to under 60 KB each. The
screenshots are matched to the stage they show (the source had them
swapped). Flag adminUserJourney, on for staging and production as asked.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Je1v64McNyB6XEu6gFgM4C
